==English==

===Etymology===
1670s, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|subtrahendus}} {{m|la|numerus||number to be subtracted}}, form of {{m|la|subtrahō||I pull out from under, I subtract}} (English {{m|en|subtract}}).<ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary}}</ref>

Surface analysis is {{suffix|subtract|end|t2=patient (recipient) of action|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsʌbtɹəhɛnd/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|arithmetic}} A number or quantity to be subtracted from another.
#: ''In the subtraction 10 &minus; 4, 4 is the subtrahend.''

